{
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "7160a087-22e6-4fbf-9d31-1c4c9d150767",
      "name": "prometheusmetrics",
      "description": {
        "content": "prometheusmetrics is VAST's Prometheus exporter resource. Prometheus is an open-source systems monitoring and alerting toolkit that provides a data model for describing and recording metrics over time and also provides a web application to display those metrics. Prometheus can be configured to fetch metrics from a third party system (such as in this case VAST Cluster) by means of a software entity called a Prometheus exporter. A Prometheus exporter collects metrics from a third party system, converts them to Prometheus metrics and exposes them via a resource path. The VAST prometheus exporter can fetch pre-defined metrics from the VMS database and return the data as a plain/text key-value format response.  You can configure the Prometheus server to scrape the metrics from the exporter at a chosen interval and display the VMS metrics through its display applications.",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
